\document[lang=en-GB]
\meta[title="Quarterly Report", author="Finance"]
\section[size=A4, margins=2cm]

\image[width=6cm, alt="wordgenx logo"]{img/logo.png}

= Quarterly Report

A pipe table is the quickest way to write a table:

| Region | Q1 | Q2 |
| North  | 10.5 | 12.25 |
| South  | 8 | 9.75 |

\table[header-rows=1, widths=(5cm, 1fr, 1fr), columns=(left, right, right), align=center]{
  | Line item          | Q3 2026  | Q3 2025  |
  | Revenue            | 48,210   | 44,067   |
  | Cost of services   | (35,980) | (31,950) |
  | \cell[colspan=3, align=center, shade=#FFF2CC]{*Operating income: 5,690*} |||
}

The block form takes any content in a cell, with merged cells, shading and row options:

\table[widths=(4cm, 1fr)]{
  \row[header]{ \cell[shade=#1F6FB2]{\font[color=#FFFFFF]{*Item*}} \cell[shade=#1F6FB2]{\font[color=#FFFFFF]{*Description*}} }
  \row{
    \cell[rowspan=2, valign=center]{Merged over two rows}
    \cell{
      A first paragraph.

      - a list inside a cell
      - with \b{formatting}
    }
  }
  \row[height=(1.2cm, at-least), cant-split]{
    \cell{A nested table: \image[height=0.6cm]{img/logo.png}

      | a | b |
      | c | d |
    }
  }
}

No borders: \image[width=25%, alt="small logo"]{img/logo.png}

\table[style=none, widths=(1fr, 1fr)]{
  | Signed: | Date: |
}
